<title>BELGIUM: W.Europe car registrations up 9.3 pct in April.</title>
<headline>W.Europe car registrations up 9.3 pct in April.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are provisional West European new car registrations and market share figures for April released by the European Automobile Manufacturers Association (ACEA).</p>
<p>Brand		  April 97   pct change  mkt share vs April 96</p>
<p>							   (pct)	 (pct)</p>
<p>All brands	   1,272,100    +9.3</p>
<p>Volkswagen	     227,200   +10.4	   17.9	 17.7</p>
<p>Fiat		     159,900   +23.0	   12.6	 11.2</p>
<p>GM			 155,013    +3.4	   12.2	 12.9</p>
<p>Ford		     141,102    +6.0	   11.1	 11.4</p>
<p>PSA			139,366    +2.2	   11.0	 11.7</p>
<p>Japanese		 139,594    +6.3	   11.0	 11.3</p>
<p>Renault		  126,725   +13.4	   10.0	  9.6</p>
<p>BMW			 77,874   +11.2	    6.1	  6.0</p>
<p>Mercedes		  50,200   +20.0	    3.9	  3.6</p>
<p>Korean		    21,414    -4.5	    1.7	  1.9</p>
<p>Volvo		     22,670   +31.1	    1.8	  1.5</p>
<p>NOTE - (Volkswagen includes Audi, Seat, Skoda; GM includes Opel/Vauxhall, U.S. imports  aUSGIM/A, Saab, IBC /ISUZU ; Ford includes U.S. imports, Jaguar; Fiat includes Lancia, Alfa Romeo, Innocenti, Ferrari, Maserati; PSA includes Peugeot, Citroen; Japanese includes Nissan, Toyota, Mazda, Honda, Mitsubishi, others; BMW includes Rover; ACEA provides no breakdown for the Korean figures.)</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6811</p>
